[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114981,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 180,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Familial gigantiform cementoma (FGC) is a rare benign fibro-osseous lesion of the jaws, characterized by an early onset and multifocal grossly expansile growth.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:31:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114982,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 180,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:31:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114983,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 180,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E83.0 &amp; XH6W94 Benign osteogenic tumours of bone or articular cartilage of skull or face &amp; Gigantiform cementoma</p>\r\n<p>2E83.1 &amp; XH6W94 Benign osteogenic tumours of bone or articular cartilage of lower jaw &amp; Gigantiform cementoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:31:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114984,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 180,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> gigantiform cementoma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> florid osseous dysplasia, expansive osseous dysplasia.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:31:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114985,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 180,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:31:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114986,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 180,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The disease affects the jaws, with multifocal involvement in two to four quadrants {25409854}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:31:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114987,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 180,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is rapidly progressive, painless expansion, resulting in significant deformity, orbital distortion, and possible airway compromise {10077086; 11312460; 25409854}. Many cases of florid cemento-osseous dysplasia have been diagnosed as FGC, particularly cases of the familial form {32315206}, but the degree of expansion is usually less marked and patients are generally older {27161103}. Presentations of gnathodiaphysial dysplasia and large cemento-ossifying fibromas are also often mistaken for FGC.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>Radiographic examination shows well-defined, markedly expansile radiolucencies with associated calcifications; lesions often cross the midline {11312460; 21830054; 25409854}. Features of cemento-osseous dysplasia should be absent.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:31:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114988,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 180,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FGC is extremely rare {26945411}. Onset is in early childhood, with continuous growth into early adulthood {25409854}. Cases have been described in various countries, with 55% from Asia.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:31:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114989,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 180,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology is unknown. Autosomal dominant inheritance with a high level of penetrance and variable expressivity {25409854} has been proposed; other cases are sporadic {11312460; 25284619}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:31:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114990,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 180,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:31:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114991,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 180,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lobular mineralized masses {22378756}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:31:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114992,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 180,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The histopathological features are similar to those of cemento-ossifying fibroma and other fibro-osseous lesions. Immature bony trabeculae and cementum-like calcifications are seen within a hypercellular fibroblastic stroma. The cementum-like calcifications appear as hypocellular, spheroidal to curvilinear structures, which may be surrounded by radiating Sharpey fibres as visualized under polarized light {25409854}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:31:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114993,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 180,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:31:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114994,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 180,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:31:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114995,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 180,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> onset in childhood or adolescence; multifocal/multiquadrant involvement; very marked expansion; benign fibro-osseous histology analogous to cemento-ossifying fibroma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> rapid progression followed by slower growth later in life; family history.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:31:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114996,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 180,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:31:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114997,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 180,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Surgical management is complicated by extensive disease and rapid regrowth; complete resection is often not practical {26945411}. Surgical recontouring or partial excision typically results in regrowth, which may occur at an accelerated rate. Although the condition is characterized by a rapidly progressive growth phase, spontaneous stabilization may occur later in life {25284619}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T12:31:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]